@startuml OAuth2 Flow Sequence Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
    BorderColor #6C757D
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
    BorderColor #FFC107
}

title Gmail OAuth2 Authentication Flow

actor "User" as User
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant "FastAPI App" as API
participant "GmailAuthManager" as AuthMgr
participant "Google OAuth2" as Google
participant "Gmail API" as Gmail
participant "File System" as FS

== Initial Setup ==
User -> Browser: Navigate to application
Browser -> API: GET /auth/status
API -> FS: Check if token.json exists
FS -> API: File not found
API -> Browser: {"authenticated": false, "login_url": "/auth/login"}
Browser -> User: Show "Login Required"

== OAuth2 Login Flow ==
User -> Browser: Click "Login with Gmail"
Browser -> API: GET /auth/login

activate API
API -> AuthMgr: get_authorization_url()
activate AuthMgr

AuthMgr -> AuthMgr: Create OAuth2 Flow
note right: Uses client_secret.json\nSets redirect_uri, scopes

AuthMgr -> Google: Generate authorization URL
Google -> AuthMgr: authorization_url + state
AuthMgr -> API: Return (authorization_url, state)
deactivate AuthMgr

API -> API: Store state globally
note right: oauth_state = state\n(Security verification)

API -> Browser: RedirectResponse(authorization_url)
deactivate API

Browser -> Google: Redirect to Google OAuth consent screen

== User Consent ==
Google -> User: Show consent screen
note right: Permissions requested:\n- gmail.readonly\n- gmail.modify

User -> Google: Grant permissions
Google -> Browser: Redirect with authorization code
Browser -> API: GET /auth/callback?code=AUTH_CODE&state=STATE

== Token Exchange ==
activate API
API -> API: Verify state parameter
note right: Security check:\nif state != oauth_state:\n  raise HTTPException

API -> AuthMgr: exchange_code_for_tokens(code, state)
activate AuthMgr

AuthMgr -> AuthMgr: Create OAuth2 Flow
AuthMgr -> Google: Exchange code for tokens
activate Google
Google -> Google: Validate authorization code
Google -> AuthMgr: Return access_token + refresh_token
deactivate Google

AuthMgr -> FS: Save tokens to token.json
note right: {"token": "access_token",\n "refresh_token": "refresh_token",\n "token_uri": "...",\n "client_id": "...",\n "scopes": [...]}

FS -> AuthMgr: Tokens saved
AuthMgr -> API: Return credentials object
deactivate AuthMgr

== Service Initialization ==
API -> API: Check if gmail_service exists
API -> AuthMgr: Create GmailService(auth_manager)
API -> API: Set app.state.gmail_service

== Gmail Watch Setup ==
API -> API: setup_gmail_watch(app)
API -> AuthMgr: get_credentials()
AuthMgr -> FS: Load token.json
FS -> AuthMgr: Return saved tokens
AuthMgr -> API: Valid credentials

API -> Gmail: Setup push notifications
note right: Watch request:\n{"labelIds": ["INBOX"],\n "topicName": "projects/.../topics/gmail-notifications",\n "labelFilterBehavior": "INCLUDE"}

Gmail -> API: Watch confirmation + expiration
API -> Browser: {"message": "Authentication successful! Gmail monitoring is now active."}
deactivate API

Browser -> User: Show success message

== Subsequent API Calls ==
User -> Browser: Make Gmail API request
Browser -> API: GET /gmail/messages
API -> AuthMgr: get_credentials()

activate AuthMgr
AuthMgr -> FS: Load token.json
FS -> AuthMgr: Return tokens
AuthMgr -> AuthMgr: Check if token expired

alt Token Valid
    AuthMgr -> API: Return valid credentials
else Token Expired
    AuthMgr -> Google: Refresh token request
    Google -> AuthMgr: New access token
    AuthMgr -> FS: Update token.json
    AuthMgr -> API: Return refreshed credentials
end
deactivate AuthMgr

API -> Gmail: Authenticated API call
Gmail -> API: Response data
API -> Browser: JSON response
Browser -> User: Display results

== Error Scenarios ==
note over API, Google
**Error Handling:**
1. Invalid state → HTTPException(400)
2. No refresh token → Exception("Manual OAuth flow required")
3. Token refresh fails → Re-authentication needed
4. Gmail API errors → HTTP 500 with error details
end note

@enduml